        "fr-extract.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "32330577-5c64-3af1-b5f0-76ff9d456f8c",
                "word": "blockchain",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "f1c5c01d-1acb-49de-903c-3c897f477cd0",
                        "entry_id": "32330577-5c64-3af1-b5f0-76ff9d456f8c",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "blockchains"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "af9bd263-7bdc-306f-b9c8-8e9170cbc6fe",
                        "entry_id": "32330577-5c64-3af1-b5f0-76ff9d456f8c",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Chaine de blocs."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "e67b9c19-8bbd-4919-ab82-37bebf79e37c",
                                "sense_id": "af9bd263-7bdc-306f-b9c8-8e9170cbc6fe",
                                "text": "Blockchain is a much-discussed instrument that, according to some, promises to inaugurate a new era of data storage and code-execution, which could, in turn, stimulate new business models and markets. The precise impact of the technology is, of course, hard to anticipate with certainty, in particular as many remain sceptical of blockchain 's potential impact."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "6b3e960a-bd3e-415f-97f7-fd1aca878047",
                                "sense_id": "af9bd263-7bdc-306f-b9c8-8e9170cbc6fe",
                                "text": "Blockchains, however, are distributed databases that often seek to achieve decentralisation by replacing a unitary actor with many different players. The lack of consensus as to how (joint-) controllership ought to be defined hampers the allocation of responsibility and accountability."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
